# the jump to a function that calls a parameter last is owed only because of what may arrive there: where the call hands over a closure made here whose function ends its tail calls, it may come back
# f5 = maker, which returns last(toLeaf, v). f11 = both, which meets both conditions of either. f14 = outer, which hands toMaker to passes, and passes hands it on to last
# f3 = passes hands on its own parameter, f7 = round and f16 = spin stand on rings through their closures, f9 = blind hands over a closure with a condition of its own, f12 = oneOfTwo meets one condition of two
# RUN: walk f5 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK: [[call]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f2
# CHECK: ReturnCall [[call]] {{*}}requirement=Allowed
# RUN(BOTH): walk f11 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# BOTH-LABEL: code f11:Body
# BOTH: [[call]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f10
# BOTH: ReturnCall [[call]] {{*}}requirement=Allowed
# RUN(OUTER): walk f14 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# OUTER-LABEL: code f14:Body
# OUTER: [[call]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f3
# OUTER: ReturnCall [[call]] {{*}}requirement=Allowed
# RUN(OWED): walk f7 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# OWED-LABEL: code f7:Body
# OWED: [[call]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f2
# OWED: ReturnCall [[call]]
# RUN(NEVER): walk f3 f7 f9 f12 f16 mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# NEVER-NOT: requirement=Allowed
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../plan/tail-calls/function-that-calls-a-parameter-last-ends-its-tail-calls-if-what-arrives-does.ir
